  "description": "Build-first origination gate. FIVE facts (per @pipavlo82): (1) content identity, (2) existence witness, (3) anchor subject binding, (4) thread subject binding — the thread witness is THIS proposal's OPENING boundary: the resolved forge_event PR must ADD the proposal's spec file (status=='added'), so a later amendment that merely MODIFIES it does not bind, and all PR-file pages are read or the resolver fails closed, (5) witnessed precedence. `resolution` is a MODEL INPUT (companion resolve_anchor.py produces + enforces it): {anchor:{content,witness_declared,witnessed_ts,subject_bound}, thread:{witnessed,witnessed_ts,subject_bound}}. The thread witness must also sit in the proposal's CANONICAL repository (erc->ethereum/ERCs, eip->ethereum/EIPs) — enforced in BOTH the deterministic gate (a non-canonical repo returns thread_not_bound regardless of a resolution claiming subject_bound=true) and the live resolver — and the spec path is matched EXACT-CASE (ERCS/erc-<id>.md), so a spoof repo or a case-variant path cannot impersonate the opening. The record carries `proposal` {kind,id}. Gate checks coherence, fails closed on a non-object/non-dict record or resolution, rejects bool where int is required. REAL rows: every row referencing ethereum/ERCs PRs 1810/1826/1932 carries that PR's EXACT GitHub created_at (1781183206 / 1781874038 / 1786012951), and only the on-chain 8299 (0xc3aeb16d…) and 8373 (0x04e1846f…) anchors are real. SYNTHETIC rows: proposal id >= 90000 and PR >= 990000 are ordering controls (postdates) with fabricated times, not presented as real PRs; the witnessed-8309 PASS and all witness tx values (0x0000…/0x1111…/…) are opaque model fixtures. Counts: 3 PASS, 12 FAIL, 12 UNVERIFIABLE = 27. Proves witnessed temporal + existence only, never semantic origination.",
